w: 1.~Praise ye the Lord: with my whole heart I will God's praise de- clare, Where the as- sem- blies of the just and cong- re- ga- tions are.
w: * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
w: 3.~His work most ho- nou- ra- ble is, most glo- ri- ous and pure, And his un- tain- ted right- eous- ness for ev- er doth en- dure.
w: 4.~His works most won- der- ful he hath made to be thought up- on: The Lord is gra- cious, and he is full o- f com- pas- sion.
w: 5.~He gi- veth meat un- to all those that tru- ly do him fear; And ev- er- more his cov- e- nant he in his mind will bear.
w: 6.~He did the po- wer of his works un- to his peo- ple show, When he the hea- then's he- ri- tage up- on them did be- stow.
w: 7.~His han- dy\-- works are truth and right; all his com- mands are sure: And, done in truth and u- prigh- tness, they ev- er- more en- dure.
w: 8.~He sent re- demp- tion to his folk; his cov- e- nant for aye He did com- mand: ho- ly his name and rev'- rend is al- way.
w: 9.~Wis- dom's be- gin- ning is God's fear: good un- der- stand- ing they Have all that his com- mands ful- fill: his praise en- dures for aye.
